@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+# Device Library bridge
+
+This Nova modification adds a FrontendLayer-owned QObject exposed as `deviceLibrary` to QML. Local actions and the last complete snapshot are stored in SQLite. Pending actions survive restart and are retained on conflicts. Launch commands remain outside this bridge.
+
+Sync is optional. Without enrollment the local catalogue and theme remain usable; remote synchronization is unavailable. The server implementation and personal data are not part of this source distribution.
+
+Enrollment uses an HTTPS base URL, a device ID and a device-scoped capability. Android loads app-private enrollment and encrypts it with Android Keystore. Linux obtains capabilities through Secret Service rather than a plaintext token file. `DEVICE_LIBRARY_DIR` optionally selects a private absolute directory on Linux; `DEVICE_LIBRARY_DEVICE_ID` checks enrollment identity. No sample credentials or device-specific setup files are supplied.
+
+Snapshots reject executable and credential fields, foreign device identity, incomplete v1 data and oversized payloads. Unknown duration and progress remain unknown. Server availability is last-known evidence, not proof that a local file or launch route works. Redirects are not followed. Plain HTTP is restricted to explicitly configured shared-address-space transport; use HTTPS for portable deployments.
+
+Build the synthetic offline harness outside the source tree with a compatible Qt development installation:
+
+```sh
+mkdir device-library-test-build
+cd device-library-test-build
+qmake ../src/backend/library/tests.pro
+make -j2
+./device-library-tests
+```
+
+On macOS, qmake may create an app bundle whose binary is `device-library-tests.app/Contents/MacOS/device-library-tests`. The harness covers durable offline actions, idempotency, conflicts, revision predictions, malformed snapshot preservation, endpoint policy and enrollment checks. See the Nova repository validation notes for the proof layer actually exercised.
